$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh --version
yubikey-db-migrate.sh 1.1.0
[exit 0]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh 
Usage: yubikey-db-migrate.sh [options] SQLITE_FILE

Copy the users and YubiKeys from a yubikey-db.sh SQLite database into its
PostgreSQL database, in one transaction, verified row by row.

Options:
  -d, --db NAME                 PostgreSQL database (default: yubikey)
  -m, --mode MODE               new (default): the PostgreSQL table must be empty
                                sync: add missing keys and move counters forward
  -e, --secret-encoding ENC     How AES keys are stored in PostgreSQL:
                                base64 (default) | hex (match yubikey-db.sh -e)
  -n, --dry-run                 Do everything, then roll back: nothing changes
      --skip-invalid            Migrate the valid rows even if some are invalid
  -h, --help                    Show this help
  -V, --version                 Show the version

PostgreSQL connections use the standard PGHOST, PGPORT, PGUSER, PGSSLMODE and
PGSERVICE settings. Keep passwords in ~/.pgpass.
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh --mode copy src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: --mode must be new or sync
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh -e rot13 src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: --secret-encoding must be base64 or hex
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh --bogus src.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: unknown option '--bogus' (see 'yubikey-db-migrate.sh --help')
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh a.db b.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: only one SQLite file allowed
[exit 1]

$ yubikey-db-migrate.sh <WORK>/missing.db
yubikey-db-migrate.sh: error: cannot read <WORK>/missing.db
[exit 1]

